WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.900
TSM Intelligence Platform connects workforce intelligence, frontline operations, enterprise systems and executive decision-making through one architecture, in the real application. We start with Workforce Intelligence.

2
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:24.900
This view switches between two preset workforce scenarios, each with its own readiness and compliance configuration. That is a demo configuration, not a live candidate lookup.

3
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:33.400
That intelligence has to reach the point where work actually happens: the L one Ticket Copilot, running in the real application.

4
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:45.000
An offboarding ticket is entered. TSM classifies the task type and shows closure as blocked, because the required evidence is not in yet. The technician decides what happens next.

5
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.000
The same intelligence pattern extends into the enterprise, in the SAP Strategist.

6
00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:01.100
Starting the journey traces a business object across commerce, CRM, master data, CPQ, approval and downstream operations.

7
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:10.400
Instead of viewing each system on its own, TSM shows the relationships between them: the business object trace, stage by stage.

8
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:16.700
The same data condition can propagate across multiple application boundaries downstream.

9
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:24.700
The enterprise impact view shows that propagation across systems, not just the health of one application on its own.

10
00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:35.100
The strategist assembles the evidence needed for an executive decision. The decision itself stays a business action: investigate, remediate, or escalate.

11
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:47.400
The Operational OS brings recovery data into one executive package once a case is selected. This environment has no case connected yet, so the package view is shown empty, honestly.

12
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:58.900
Human decision, action, evidence, outcome: that is the loop at the center of TSM, from workforce intelligence through frontline execution to the executive view, and back again.

